# Cursor Rules — [Project Name]

# SOPs (canonical)
# Full procedures: DOCS/RULE.md
# Doc-sync / backup workflow: DOCS/claude.md → "SOP-DOC"

# Documentation
- Update DOCS/ when making architectural or behavioral changes.
- Before significant releases or pushes, run SOP-DOC in claude.md (prompt audit → drift → core docs → commit/push as appropriate).
- Keep CHANGELOG.md, CONFIGURATION_MANAGEMENT.md, and bugtracker/ aligned with code changes.

# Code style
- Follow existing conventions in the codebase.
- Prefer readability and maintainability over cleverness.

# Bug tracking
- Before risky changes (auth, payments, export/import, core UX), skim DOCS/bugtracker/bug_tracker.md and relevant records.
- Add a bug record in DOCS/bugtracker/records/ when fixing a non-trivial bug.
- Link fixes to CHANGELOG or "Recent code changes" when your project uses that table.

# LLM / prompts (if applicable)
- When changing prompts, update PROMPT_REFERENCES.md and PROMPT_TRACKER.md per claude.md SOP-PROMPT.

# Architecture
- Respect module boundaries and data flow (see ARCHITECTURE.md).
- Do not introduce dependencies that conflict with documented architecture.
